":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"repository":{"id":43723161,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk0MzcyMzE2MQ==","name":"helm","full_name":"helm/helm","private":false,"owner":{"login":"helm","id":15859888,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE1ODU5ODg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15859888?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm","html_url":"https://github.com/helm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/helm/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm","description":"The Kubernetes Package Manager","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/deployments","created_at":"2015-10-06T01:07:32Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T12:39:30Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T21:17:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/helm/helm.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:helm/helm.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm","homepage":"https://helm.sh","size":26241,"stargazers_count":29174,"watchers_count":29174,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":7445,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":476,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":true,"topics":["chart","charts","cncf","helm","kubernetes"],"visibility":"public","forks":7445,"open_issues":476,"watchers":29174,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/pulls/6655","html_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm/pull/6655","diff_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm/pull/6655.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/helm/helm/pull/6655.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Signed-off-by: Hang Park <hangpark@kaist.ac.kr>\r\n\r\nThis PR includes the removal of checking sync status of `Chart.yaml` and `Chart.lock` dependencies before executing the main functionality of `helm dependency build`.\r\n\r\nThis resolves #6416. Moreover, similar to #6416, this resolves abnormal failures on `build` when `Chart.yaml` contains some subchart versions in the form of **SemVer range**, too.\r\n\r\nFixes #6416 \r\n\r\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\r\n\r\n- #6416 reports that `helm dependency build` command (abbr. `build`) fails if `Chart.yaml` contains subchart's alias.\r\n- I found that a same failure happens if `Chart.yaml` contains *SemVer range* on some of its subcharts.\r\n\r\nThese two bugs are originated from a mismatch of hashed digests of deps in `Chart.yaml` and `Chart.lock`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBefore #5874 merged, hashed digest in `Chart.lock` is calculated from `Chart.yaml` deps.\r\nThis makes `Chart.lock` not be updated properly when all of below happened:\r\n\r\n1. subchart's version is written in SemVer range\r\n2. that subchart is updated to a new version (still within the range)\r\n3. `helm dep up` is executed and so the new version is installed\r\n\r\nbecause it is true that the contents of `Chart.yaml` are not changed!\r\n\r\nSo, #5874 made digest calculation to use `Chart.lock` contents, not of `Chart.yaml`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBut notice that (1) lock file does not contain alias information and (2) lock file has specific *resolved* versions while yaml file may have version ranges.\r\n\r\nChecking sync on yaml & lock (actually comparing hashed digests of deps in each file) in `build` command worked well before #5874.\r\nHowever, after that PR merged, this comparing process is not valid with ranged versions (and #6416 was a bug even before #5874.)\r\n\r\nMore technically, `build` command (1) loads a chart and stores it in `var c *chart.Chart`, (2) calculates the hash value of `c.Meta.Dependencies`, and then (3) compares it with `c.Lock.Digest` value, which was already written in the `Chart.lock` file.\r\n\r\nThat `c.Lock.Digest` is originated from previous `dep update` command, which (1) loads a chart, (2) resolves deps, (3) calculates the hash value of **resolved deps**, and then (4) stores resolved deps along with its hash value as a digest into `Chart.lock` file.\r\n\r\nNote that `c.Meta.Dependencies[i].Alias` may exist but `c.Lock.Dependencies[i].Alias` is always empty, and that `c.Meta.Dependencies[i].Version` may be SemVer range but `c.Lock.Dependencies[i].Version` is just a single resolved version. (see internal/resolver/resolver.go)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Thus, I removed comparing hashed digests of two files in `build` command.**\r\n\r\n## Special notes for your reviewer\r\n\r\nMy PR is the simplest way to fix bugs I think, but there are many other approaches **without removal of comparing two files**.  For example:\r\n\r\n1. record digests of both original deps declaration and resolved lock file contents, so use one of it in each desired situation properly (we can concatenate two digests into one digest, maybe)\r\n2. instead of comparing digests, determine out-of-sync manually like: `dep_yaml.name == dep_lock.name` && `dep_yaml.repo == dep_lock.repo` && `dep_yaml.version CONTAINS dep_lock.version` && each pairs of `(name, repo)` in `Chart.yaml` APPEARS in `Chart.lock` also (and vice-versa.)\r\n\r\nIf you guys think these approaches are better than this PR, I'd like to work further on this issue.\r\n\r\n**If applicable**:\r\n- [x] this PR contains unit tests","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/issues/6655/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/helm/helm/issues/6655/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"stefanprodan","id":3797675,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTc2NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3797675?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanprodan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanprodan/received_events","type":"User",